{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782270024,"nonce":"wmUbR78GjcniVmWVYDNDoBqis8A=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGgF6gw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/319","origin":"github"},"title":"Wire bathymetry_layer into bizzyboat nav2 costmaps (Massabesic store)","message":"## Summary\n\nWire the `bathymetry_layer` Nav2 costmap plugin\n(`rolker/unh_marine_autonomy`, added in unh_marine_autonomy#216 / #164) into\n**bizzyboat's** local and global costmaps so the boat plans against the\nbathymetric store — the ingested NH GRANIT contour chart prior plus the M3 survey\ndraft — at Lake Massabesic.\n\nPart of the bathy-store effort (consumer side of rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#216).\n\n## Why bizzy's overlay (not the base)\n\n`echoboat_project11/nav2_params.base.yaml` lists `chart_layer` (s57) in both\ncostmaps, but bizzy's `nav2_overlay.yaml` **commented out `chart_layer`** (per\noperator, 2026-06-12) and restates the plugin lists wholesale (deep-merge replaces\nlists). So bizzy must be edited directly; the base is untouched.\n\n## Changes (`bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`)\n\nAdd `bathymetry_layer` to both plugin lists (before `inflation_layer`) and a config\nblock in each costmap:\n\n```yaml\nbathymetry_layer:\n  plugin: \"bathymetry_layer::BathymetryLayer\"\n  enabled: True\n  store_path: \"/home/field/data/stores/bathymetry\"\n  minimum_depth: 1.0\n  maximum_caution_depth: 2.5\n  max_uncertainty: 5.0          # see coupling note\n  max_age: 0.0\n  unsurveyed_is_lethal: True    # closed lake basin: no-data = land\n  map_tide_frame: \u003ctf_prefix\u003e/map_tide\n```\n\n## Key parameter rationale\n\n- **`unsurveyed_is_lethal: True`** — the chart prior is masked to the lake outline,\n  so no-data cells are land; mark them lethal (the #216 feature's purpose).\n- **`max_uncertainty: 5.0`** — *coupling*: the chart prior was imported with a\n  per-cell uncertainty of 5.0 m. `shallowestReliable` rejects cells with\n  `uncertainty \u003e max_uncertainty`, and a present-but-rejected cell is written\n  LETHAL. With the 0.5 m default the whole chart-covered lake would be LETHAL, so\n  this must be ≥ 5.0. (Follow-up option: re-import the chart with a lower, more\n  honest contour-interpolation uncertainty so a tighter gate can be used.)\n- **`store_path`** — `/home/field/data/stores/bathymetry` (boat `field` user data\n  root, mirroring dev `~/data/stores/bathymetry`).\n- **`map_tide_frame`** — `\u003ctf_prefix\u003e/map_tide`, matching the base chart_layer's\n  `sea_surface_frame`.\n\n## Deployment caveat (not blocking the config)\n\nThe materialized store currently lives on the dev machine\n(`~/data/stores/bathymetry`). It must be synced to the boat at\n`/home/field/data/stores/bathymetry` before the layer contributes anything; until\nthen the layer logs a one-shot error and no-ops (safe).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}